"</style></head><body style=\" font-family:'Sans Serif'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;\">\n"
"<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">There are two caches being used for Marble: The physical memory which is needed to keep map data in the computer's memory. Increasing the value will make the application more responsive. The hard disc memory cache is used by download contents from the Internet (e.g. Wikipedia data or map data). Decrease this value if you want to save space on the hard disc and if high usage of the Internet is not an issue. </p>"
"</body></html>"
msgstr ""
"<html><head><meta name=\"qrichtext\" content=\"1\" /><style type=\"text/css\">\n"
"p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }\n"
"</style></head><body style=\" font-family:'Sans Serif'; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;\">\n"
"<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">Marble bruukt twee Oorden vun Twischenspiekers: De physikaalsch Spieker för't Wohren vun Koortendaten in'n Reeknerspieker. En grötter Weert lett dat Programm gauer reageren. De Fastplatten-Twischenspieker warrt för't Daalladen vun Daten ut dat Internet (a.B. Wiki- oder Koortendaten) bruukt. Maak dissen Weert lütter, wenn Du Fastplattenplatz sporen wullt un nich faken op dat Internet togrippst.</p>"
"</body></html>"

